error[GRL009]: `inner` is used before it is defined
 --> rules/GRL009.grl:5:18
  |
5 |   def outer(x) = inner(x)
  |                  ^^^^^ used here
6 |   def inner(x) = x is call
  |       ----- defined here, after its use
  |
  = help: a def may call only the defs written above it; move `def inner` above `def outer`
  = explain: grimble explain GRL009

error[GRL009]: `walk` calls itself
 --> rules/GRL009.grl:7:31
  |
7 |   def walk(x) = x is call and walk(x)
  |                               ^^^^^^^ a def cannot recurse
  |
  = help: to follow a chain of calls use `reaches ... via calls within N`, which is bounded
  = explain: grimble explain GRL009

